        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 432,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 382,
        "paragraph_id": "1365B63A",
        "text": "A formulation of Van Thiel de Vries (2009) based on the parameterized wave shape model of Rienecker and Fenton (1981) (keyword: waveform = vanthiel)"
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 16126,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 434,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 384,
        "paragraph_id": "3AB129C4",
        "text": "The formulation of Ruessink et al. (2012) relies on parameterizations for the non-linearity parameter r and phase Φ. The parameterizations are based on a data set of 30.000+ field observations of the orbital skewness Sk and asymmetry As, collected under non-breaking and breaking wave conditions. The only variable parameter is the Ursell number, since according to Ruessink et al. (2012) the Ursell that includes Hs, T and h, describes the variability in Sk and As well. The Ursell number is calculated with the equation below."
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 16368,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 438,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 388,
        "paragraph_id": "0DFB17F5",
        "text": "The value for the skewness and asymmetry is calculated with the use of a Boltzmann sigmoid. The skewness and asymmetry are a function of Ψ. In the formulation of Ruessink et al. (2012) the p1:6 are used as parameterized factors on the data set of field observations."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_master.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 16412,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 440,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 390,
        "paragraph_id": "54B833D0",
        "text": "(2.28)"
      }
    ],
